{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-007","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as \"Polyurethene\" but calls for I.Z.B.P. (trivalent zinc plating), a metallic electroplated coating that cannot be applied to polyurethane. The designer must resolve this contradiction by either changing the material or removing/changing the surface treatment."

,
"recommended_correction":"Change the material to a metal compatible with zinc plating, or change the surface treatment to one suitable for polyurethane."}]}
